  "notes": "Karbonn SWTV-20AE (Skyworth OEM, SW4H, MediaTek), Android TV 10, firmware QTG3.200617.002\nro.product.manufacturer=skyworth, device SW4H, API 29, armeabi-v7a, ~1.68 GB RAM.\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (classic Android TV home, not Google TV launcherx).\nLive TV: com.smartdevice.livetv / com.mediatek.tvinput.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/karbonn-swtv-20ae/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/karbonn-swtv-20ae/debloat.txt com.google.android.tvlauncher\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nTested on the day of debloat and confirmed working. Same Skyworth SW4H platform as the\nPanasonic 4KTV-0SU and OnePlus Y1. com.sky.market is a protected package: the firmware\nrefuses pm disable-user for it (SecurityException); it stays on.\n\nPerformance tweaks for 1.68 GB RAM (32-bit armeabi-v7a, MediaTek):\nsettings put global window_animation_scale 0.5\nsettings put global transition_animation_scale 0.5\nsettings put global animator_duration_scale 0.5\nsettings put global background_process_limit 2\nSet reduced_motion: true in your theme's config.json for the CleanYourTV launcher.\nSkyworth content, ads and preloads",
